// `...` is the other spelling an inclusive range arrives as, so it gets the same answer as
// `..=` rather than a broken parse. Its own fixture because the lexer resolves it with a
// separate byte test — three characters, not two — and a rule tested once for two spellings
// is a rule that can silently stop covering one of them.
for i in 0...3 {
    print(i);
}
